use ./lib

from emul import Emul

export test EmulPlugin:
    expects:
        There should be an @{Emul} plugin that supports importing and
        referencing Emul.

        All emul integration must be implemented via a plugin.

export test EmulReference:
    expects:
        When importing and referencing an @{Emul} file, it should be expected
        that the emul compiler is already installed on the system, and the agent
        will generate either an SVG, a PNG, HTML, or look at the Emul file
        directly -- whatever it decides is most useful for what's currently
        being worked on.

export test LspSupport:
    expects:
        The LSP should adapt to the Emul plugin such that it understands what an
        emul import and reference are.

export test ReachFollowsEmulUses:
    expects:
        An emul-design anchor references the designs that the design extends
        or instances, also through local designs that the file does not
        export, so piton reach reaches the components of a referenced
        composition. Names in text and imports that no design uses are not
        reached.
